# Line endings — this repository is pure LF, and that is measured, not assumed.
#
# Measured 2026-10-18: `core.autocrlf` is `true` in this repo and there was no
# `.gitattributes`, so git would rewrite every text file to CRLF the next time it
# touched the working copy. That silently breaks the project's byte-truth
# discipline (`tr -cd '\r' < f | wc -c`, the check the master checklist's
# "grep -c on CR lies" warning depends on) and re-marks every measured count.
#
# Verified before pinning: not one text file in HEAD contains a CR. The only
# files that do are binaries (images, PDFs, .docx), so no text file changes.

# Everything else is LF, in the blob and in the working copy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — their CR bytes are data, never line endings. These come after the
# wildcard because the last matching rule wins. `binary` is the standard macro
# for `-diff -merge -text`, so no line-ending conversion is even attempted.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
